4. chs_rt / unsafe C on check path (note only)
========================================================================

- **Typecheck core** is pure `.oo` (`check_drive`, `tc_*`, `load_import`) — no user program linked into `chs_rt` for `oodac check`.
- **Native product host** uses runtime floor for: `read_file` / `path_exists` / `file_size` / `process_exit` / (emit probes) `sys_exec`.
- Relevant runtime coupling for **this** audit: `sys_exec` env filter **breaks** emit env probes (`EMIT_NO_CONCAT`, `PURE_NO_ARC`) — C floor side effect on emit honesty, not on typecheck soundness.
- pure multi final link **does** link `runtime/chs_rt.c` + emitted C — **after** optional check; orthogonal to multi typecheck correctness.
- No check-path buffer overflow / unsafe C ownership claimed closed or open beyond existing runtime ZT ledger.

